BayOp (Bioqore "voyager-ml-bayop")
Authors: Kai Suematsu and joshBioqore, Bioqore.
Used with the permission of its owner, the author of this repository, who
asked for the BayOp work to be taken into Kalos (recorded 2026-11-20 on branch
feat/cold-start-design). The BayOp repository has no license file of its own;
this permission is the basis for the reuse below.

What was taken:
- The idea of a model-free, space-filling first round: BayOp's Latin-hypercube
  mode (bayop_libraries/bayop_sampling.py and bayop_pipeline_states/
  lhs_state.py: 30 runs, no target needed). Kalos re-implements it in
  kalos/core/design.py and kalos/portal/design_plan.py with its own methods
  (scrambled Sobol, LHS-maximin, gap filling), constraints, setpoint snapping,
  balanced levels and honest labels. No BayOp source file is copied.
- The edge-case fixture recipe (tests/data/_generate_fixtures.py: a fabricated
  24-run, 6-setting sheet with flat-target, single-row, NaN and
  column-mismatch variants). tests/test_bayop_edge_cases.py regenerates the
  same synthetic data from the same recipe.
